# RyFlow — Cursor Rules

Never add a co-authored-by or signature line to git commit messages.
You should add a commit -s with the local user's credentials.

## Read Before You Touch

Before modifying any file, read it fully. Do not summarise, do not infer from filename. If a route has a bug, read the route file, the schema, and the relevant service before writing a single line. Read-before-touch is non-negotiable.

---

## Project Identity

RyFlow is a local-first, offline-capable AI collaboration workspace built as an Electron desktop app. Core value proposition: everything runs on your own hardware, data never leaves your machine, works without internet, and gets faster with an AMD GPU.

**This is not a cloud product. Never suggest cloud-first solutions as defaults.**

---

## Tech Stack (Do Not Deviate Without Asking)

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React 18, Vite, TailwindCSS, TipTap, Monaco, Excalidraw, D3.js, Framer Motion, Zustand, Y.js + y-webrtc, lucide-react |
| Backend | Node.js, Express, better-sqlite3, Socket.io, ws, lz-string |
| AI | Ollama (Phi-3 Mini + nomic-embed-text), Whisper.cpp, Pollinations.ai (internet-only, acknowledged gap) |
| AMD | ROCm, llama.cpp HIP backend, Ryzen AI SDK + ONNX Runtime |
| Networking | WebRTC via y-webrtc, Y.js CRDTs, mDNS/Bonjour |
| Desktop | Electron (frameless, custom titlebar, system tray, IPC via preload.js) |
| Container | Docker + Docker Compose |

**Languages:** JavaScript (existing files), TypeScript (new files only). `checkJs: false`. Do not convert existing JS files to TS.

